      "worked_solution": "The number that can be added to $23$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $23.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $23$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(23)=-23.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n23+(-23)=23-23=0\\,✓\n$$",
